    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This paper introduces a GNSS/INS/Mamba-ODO navigation framework that maps raw IMU outputs directly to 3D velocity using asymmetric sequence segmentation, multi-scale temporal modeling, and a state-space sequence learning backbone. Tested in real-world ground vehicle experiments, the method achieves a mean 3D velocity estimation error of 0.22 m/s and maintains a 3D positioning error under 0.20 m during a 120-second GNSS outage.",
